    <h1>Kiavi Review 2026</h1>
    <p class="updated">Independently written. We earn a commission if you close a loan through our links — see our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a>.</p>
    <p class="lede">Kiavi is the biggest fix-and-flip lender in America, and for most 1–4 unit investors it's the first quote worth getting. It is not the right lender for every deal. Here's the honest breakdown.</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>Kiavi (formerly LendingHome) has funded <strong>$30B+ since 2013</strong> and originated <strong>$5.5B in fix-and-flip loans in 2024</strong> — more than three times the next-largest lender. It wins on three things: <strong>speed</strong> (closings in as little as 7–10 business days), <strong>paperwork</strong> (no W-2s, tax returns, or income verification on bridge loans), and <strong>leverage</strong> (up to 95% loan-to-cost and 80% of after-repair value). New customers who apply through a partner link also get <a href="/"><strong>{{ site.offerAmount }} cash after their first closing</strong></a>.</p>

    <h2>Loan products</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>What it is</th><th>Typical terms</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Bridge / fix-and-flip</td><td>Short-term loan to buy and rehab a property</td><td>12–24 months, interest-only, ~7.75%–12%, up to 95% LTC / 80% ARV, ~$100K–$3M</td></tr>
        <tr><td>DSCR rental</td><td>30-year loan qualified on the property's rent, not your income</td><td>30-year fixed and ARM options, roughly 6.4%–9.5% depending on DSCR, LTV, and credit</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rental portfolio</td><td>One loan across 5+ rental properties</td><td>Blanket structure, terms by portfolio</td></tr>
        <tr><td>New construction</td><td>Ground-up financing for infill builds (launched 2025)</td><td>Experienced builders; terms by project</td></tr>
      </tbody>
