    <h2>What we like</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Pricing for experienced investors is among the best in hard money.</strong> Kiavi tiers pricing by your exit count in the last 24 months; 5+ exits unlocks its best rates.</li>
      <li><strong>The process is genuinely online.</strong> Soft quote in minutes with no hard credit pull, document upload and draws handled in a dashboard, and interior appraisals are often replaced by Kiavi's own valuation model on bridge loans.</li>
      <li><strong>Flip-to-rental is one ecosystem.</strong> Finish the rehab on a bridge loan, then refinance into Kiavi's 30-year DSCR loan without starting over at a new lender.</li>
      <li><strong>Scale means predictability.</strong> A lender that securitizes billions a year doesn't improvise underwriting at the closing table.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we don't</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No lending in Utah</strong>, and no 5+ unit multifamily, mixed-use, or rural property. See <a href="/faqs/what-states-does-kiavi-lend-in/">eligible states</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>~$100K minimum loan</strong> rules out many low-cost-market deals. Sub-$100K, look at RCN Capital or Groundfloor — our <a href="/kiavi-vs/">comparison pages</a> cover both.</li>
      <li><strong>First-timers don't get the headline rates.</strong> New investors are eligible, but the advertised floor pricing assumes a track record.</li>
      <li><strong>DSCR loans carry standard prepayment penalties</strong> (typically a step-down over the first 3–5 years). Normal for the product, but read the terms — details in <a href="/faqs/kiavi-prepayment-penalty/">our FAQ</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Service is dashboard-first.</strong> If you want a loan officer who answers a cell phone on Saturday, a regional lender may fit better.</li>
    </ul>

    {% include "partials/cta.njk" %}

    <h2>Is Kiavi legit?</h2>
    <p>Yes — this question mostly comes from the hard-money price tag, not the company. Kiavi is licensed (NMLS #1125207, California Finance Lender), institutionally backed, and has operated since 2013. Double-digit rates on bridge loans are the product category, not a scam signal. Full answer: <a href="/faqs/is-kiavi-legit/">Is Kiavi legit?</a></p>

    <h2>Who should use Kiavi</h2>
    <p><strong>Use Kiavi if:</strong> you're flipping or BRRRR-ing 1–4 unit properties at $100K+ loan sizes, you value closing speed, and you want bridge and 30-year DSCR under one roof. <strong>Look elsewhere if:</strong> your deals are under $100K (RCN, Groundfloor), you're in Utah, or you're building 5+ unit multifamily (Lima One). Compare directly: <a href="/kiavi-vs/">Kiavi vs. the field</a>.</p>

    <h2>Bottom line</h2>
    <p>Kiavi earns its market share: fast, predictable, well-priced for experienced investors, and honest about being a tech-first lender. Get the soft quote (it's free and doesn't touch your credit), compare it against one regional lender, and if Kiavi wins, make sure you start through <a href="{{ site.affiliateLink }}" rel="sponsored noopener" target="_blank">the partner link</a> so the {{ site.offerAmount }} new-customer bonus attaches to your account.</p>
